<div class="stonetop-weather-pick">

  <p class="stonetop-weather-intro">
    Pick the season (per your latest <em>Seasons Change</em>), then roll 1d6 on its table, or
    choose the weather yourself.
  </p>

  {{#if clock}}
  <p class="stonetop-weather-clock">
    <i class="fas fa-hourglass-half"></i>
    Stonetop is in <strong>{{clock.label}}</strong>, {{clock.yearLabel}}{{#if clock.followed}}: its table is selected below{{else}}, but you&rsquo;ve chosen a different table{{/if}}.
  </p>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="stonetop-weather-seasons">
    {{#each seasons}}
    {{!-- `is-off-clock` only ever rides along with `is-active`: it is the selection going red
          because the season chosen is not the one the steading's clock is in. --}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-season{{#if isActive}} is-active{{/if}}{{#if isOffClock}} is-off-clock{{/if}}"
            data-season="{{key}}">{{label}}</button>
    {{/each}}
  </div>

  {{!-- The rows are BUTTONS, not list items. They were already drawn as six boxed options and
        the window was the only place in the system where that shape did nothing when clicked;
        now a click stands the row up as the weather, the same as a roll landing on it. Real
        buttons rather than clickable <li>s, so the keyboard reaches them for free and
        `aria-pressed` can say which one is standing.

        `data-index` is the position in the season's own rows array, and that is safe here in a
        way it would not be on a list the template may reorder: this one is printed in the
        book's order, straight off WEATHER_SEASONS, and the handler resolves the index against
        that same array. A season change rebuilds the whole list and clears the pick with it. --}}
  <div class="stonetop-weather-rows">
    {{#each rows}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-row{{#if isPicked}} is-picked{{/if}}"
            data-index="{{index}}" aria-pressed="{{#if isPicked}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}">
      <span class="stonetop-weather-row-range">{{range}}</span>
      <span class="stonetop-weather-row-text">{{text}}{{#if reroll}} <em class="stonetop-weather-row-reroll">(roll again later with disadvantage)</em>{{/if}}</span>
    </button>
    {{/each}}
  </div>

  {{!-- One button until there is a result, two once there is. Re-roll sits LEFT of Post, the
        wizard's Back/Next hand rather than the dialog's affirmative-left one: these are not a
        yes and a no, they are "again" and "done", and the one that ends the window belongs at
        the end of the row. Nothing here is a cancel — the window's own X is that. --}}
  <div class="stonetop-weather-roll-wrap">
    {{#if picked}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-reroll-btn">
      <i class="fas fa-rotate-right"></i> Re-roll
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-post-btn">
      <i class="fas fa-cloud-sun-rain"></i> Post the weather
    </button>
    {{else}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-roll-btn">
      <i class="fas fa-cloud-sun-rain"></i> Roll the weather
    </button>
    {{/if}}
  </div>

  {{!-- The canvas control (WeatherDialog#_fxControl), present only for a GM whose world has
        FXMaster or FXMaster+ in it. Everything above decides what the weather IS; this decides
        whether the players' map hears about it, which is why it sits under the footer behind a
        rule rather than becoming a third button in a row where the other two are still waiting
        to be pressed. It is also the only control in the window that acts immediately.

        No disabled state to paint: the row is absent, rather than dimmed, for a table with no
        particle module. --}}
  {{#if fx}}
  <div class="stonetop-weather-fx">
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-fx-btn{{#if fx.paused}} is-paused{{/if}}">
      <i class="fas {{#if fx.paused}}fa-play{{else}}fa-pause{{/if}}"></i> {{fx.label}}
    </button>
    {{!-- Text, not a button: it does nothing to the weather, it leaves for core's Configure
          Settings, where the same switch lives permanently alongside the rest of Stonetop's
          options. The window stays open behind it. --}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-weather-fx-link"
            title="Open Configure Settings at Stonetop&rsquo;s weather options">Weather settings</button>
    <span class="stonetop-weather-fx-hint">{{fx.hint}}</span>
  </div>
  {{/if}}

</div>
